		<body>
<div xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0"><head n="1" coords="1,72.0,400.0,100.0,10.0">Introduction</head><p coords="1,72.0,420.0,450.0,60.0"><s coords="1,72.0,420.0,450.0,9.0">Transformers dominate sequence modelling <ref type="bibr" target="#b1">(Vaswani et al., 2017)</ref>.</s><s coords="2,72.0,90.0,450.0,9.0">Prior work pruned heads by weight magnitude <ref type="bibr" target="#b2">[2,</ref><ref type="bibr" target="#b3">3]</ref>.</s><note place="foot" n="1">Code is available online.</note></p></div>
<div xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0"><head n="2">Methods</head></div>
<div xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0"><head n="2.1" coords="2,72.0,200.0,100.0,10.0">Data</head><p coords="2,72.0,220.0,450.0,30.0"><s coords="2,72.0,220.0,450.0,9.0">We use the standard benchmark with 12 tasks.</s></p><formula xml:id="formula_0" coords="2,72.0,260.0,300.0,20.0">L = -sum log p(x)</formula><p coords="2,72.0,290.0,450.0,30.0"><s coords="2,72.0,290.0,450.0,9.0">The loss is minimised with Adam.</s></p></div>
<div xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0"><head n="3" coords="3,72.0,100.0,100.0,10.0">Results</head><p coords="3,72.0,120.0,450.0,30.0"><s coords="3,72.0,120.0,450.0,9.0">Removing five percent of heads reduces accuracy by 12 points.</s></p></div>
